            <ArticleTitle>Touch the pain away: new research on therapeutic touch and persons with fibromyalgia syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>142-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This pilot study tested the effectiveness of 6 therapeutic touch treatments on the experience of pain and quality of life for persons with fibromyalgia syndrome. Its findings support that subjects who received therapeutic touch had a statistically significant decrease in pain for each pretherapeutic to posttherapeutic touch treatment, as well as significant improvement in quality of life from pre-first to pre-sixth treatment. Therapeutic touch may be an effective treatment for relieving pain and improving quality of life in this specific population of persons with fibromyalgia syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
